course: dictionary
lesson: 384
title: Apart: space and separation
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Apart is a small word with a big job: it tells you that things are not together. It can mean with space between, as in «far apart», or into pieces, as in «it fell apart». The words around it show you which meaning fits.
explain: «A tiger's skin is striped under the fur, and no two tigers have the same stripes, so scientists tell them apart from camera photos.» Here apart comes after tell, and it means seeing the difference between two things. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "scientists can see the difference between them from camera photos" still makes sense.
explain: Apart can also mean except, or not counting. «Apart from the rain, the day was lovely» means the day was lovely with one thing left out, the rain. Always ask what the sentence is about, then choose the meaning that makes sense.
fact: Apart is an adverb, and it often describes how things are placed or separated.
fact: «Apart» means away from each other, with space between: «far apart».
fact: «Apart» can also mean into pieces: «it fell apart».
fact: «Apart from» means except, or not counting: «Apart from Sam, everyone came.»
fact: «Tell apart» means to see the difference between two things: «Scientists tell tigers apart by their stripes.»
exercise: «The two houses stood far apart on the empty hill.» What does apart mean here? | *With a lot of space between them | Very close together | Into pieces | Except for one
exercise: «The old toy fell apart in my hands.» What does apart mean here? | Very quickly | Except for one | *Into pieces | Painted red
exercise: Jayden says, «Apart from Sam, nobody was late.» What does apart from mean? | In pieces | *Except Sam | Before Sam | Away from Sam, far off
test: Ben says, «I can tell the twins apart by their voices.» What does tell apart mean? | Lose sight of | *See the difference between them | Hide from | Make them louder
test: «The rumour fell apart by the second question.» What does fell apart mean? | Was sold for money | Grew bigger and stronger | *Broke down and did not hold together | Was spoken loudly
exam: Which meaning of apart fits «Apart from the rain, the day was lovely»? | Very loudly | *Except, not counting | Into pieces | Far away from each other
